#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:2
msgid "bool-file interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `bool-file` interface allows access to a specific class of file that "
"contains boolean semantics, typically used to toggle or represent the state "
"of binary hardware values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"This interface is primarily intended to be used with {ref}`Ubuntu Core <ref-"
"glossary_ubuntu-core>` devices, it's also restricted because it provides "
"privileged access to hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:8
msgid ""
"These kinds of file are located within specific directories inside the "
"[sysfs](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man5/sysfs.5.html) filesystem (`/"
"sys`) and this  interface allows a file to be _read_, to obtaining a current "
"value, or _written to_, setting a new value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The [LED class](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/leds/leds-class.html) "
"is a good example of file type for this interface, as it potentially allows "
"LEDs to be turned on and off, and have their brightness modified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"Use the  `snap interface bool-file` command to see which boolean files are "
"available on the system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"$ snap interface bool-file\n"
"name:    bool-file\n"
"summary: allows access to specific file with bool semantics\n"
"slots:\n"
"  - my-gadget:green-led\n"
"  - my-gadget:red-led\n"
"[...]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:25
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:28
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:28
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:31
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:34
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:35
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:71
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:74
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:30
msgid "**Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:31
msgid ""
"`path` (slot): path to the file in _sysfs_</br>   Example: `/sys/class/leds/"
"green/brightness`</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:34
msgid ""
"The path value must match one of the following regular expressions:</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:35
msgid "For GPIO devices: `^/sys/class/gpio/gpio[0-9]+/value$`</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:37
msgid "For LED devices: `^/sys/class/leds/[^/]+/brightness$`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:39
msgid ""
"The {ref}`gpio interface <interfaces-gpio-interface>`  provides another "
"option for accessing GPIO devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:41
msgid ""
"To use a boolean file, the snap developer must add `plugs: [ bool-file ]` to "
"a snap's [snapcraft.yaml](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/"
"reference/project-file/anatomy-of-snapcraft-yaml/). The snap user can then "
"access a specific boolean file with an {ref}`interface connection "
"<explanation-interfaces-all-about-interfaces>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:43
msgid ""
"Unless a snap specifically expects a set of boolean files that cannot be "
"predefined, the recommended approach is to define distinct plugs for each "
"boolean file the snap wishes to use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:45
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  green-led:\n"
"    interface: bool-file\n"
"  red-led:\n"
"    interface: bool-file\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:53
msgid ""
"Defining distinct plugs for each boolean file has the advantage of being "
"self-documenting, and 1:1  connections like these are easier to track and "
"setup with {ref}`auto-connections <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-"
"connection>`, if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:55
msgid ""
"Once connected, the consuming snap can use the boolean file via the path "
"mentioned in the `path` attribute specified by the connected slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:57
msgid "The slot side on a gadget snap may be declared as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bool-file-interface.md:59
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  green-led:\n"
"    interface: bool-file\n"
"    path: /sys/class/leds/green0/brightness\n"
"  red-led:\n"
"    interface: bool-file\n"
"    path: /sys/class/leds/red0/brightness\n"
msgstr ""

